    "body": "## Motivation\n\n`--kv-cache-dtype mxfp8` (SM100 and newer) stores the KV cache as fp8 rows plus a scale factor per 32-element block. The default pool keeps both in `MHATokenToKVPoolMXFP8`, and the FA4 MXFP8 attention path reads the scales from the pool. The unified memory pool (`--enable-unified-memory`) builds only the fp8 rows: `MHAView` leaves `k_scale_buffer` and `v_scale_buffer` as `None`. So the combination passes the boot checks and has no scale buffers for the kernel to read.\n\nThe FP4 KV cache already refuses `--enable-unified-memory` at boot for the same reason (`handle_kv4_compatibility`).\n\n## Modifications\n\n- `handle_mxfp8_kv_cache_compatibility` (`arg_groups/kv_cache_hook.py`) now raises a `ValueError` when `--kv-cache-dtype mxfp8` is combined with `--enable-unified-memory`, after its existing SM100 check. The message names the flag and the reason. MXFP8 without unified memory is unchanged.\n\nTest (CPU), `test/registered/unit/server_args/test_server_args.py`: `TestMXFP8KVCacheCompatibility::test_mxfp8_rejects_unified_memory` overrides the platform to SM100 and checks that mxfp8 alone resolves and that mxfp8 with `--enable-unified-memory` raises. It fails on main and passes with this PR.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nNot applicable: the change refuses a configuration while resolving server arguments.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nNot applicable.\n\nThe runtime failure itself needs an SM100 GPU and was not reproduced for this PR; the test covers the boot check.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format your code according to the [Format code with pre-commit](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#format-code-with-pre-commit).\n- [x] Add unit tests according to the [Run and add unit tests](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#run-and-add-unit-tests).\n- [ ] Update documentation according to [Write documentations](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#write-documentations).\n- [ ] Provide accuracy and speed benchmark results according to [Test the accuracy](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#test-the-accuracy) and [Benchmark the speed](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#benchmark-the-speed).\n- [x] Follow the SGLang code style [guidance](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#code-style-guidance).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #41537543446](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41537543446)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #41537543506](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41537543506)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #41537543258](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41537543258)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n\n> [!TIP]\n> Base CI only covers the core cases, and its workload may not exercise your change. Use `/rerun-test` to run the tests your change touches, or copy this prompt for an agent:\n>\n> ```text\n> Find the registered tests this PR affects and run them with /rerun-test, following https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/.agents/skills/rerun-test/SKILL.md\n> ```\n<!-- pr-states:end -->\n",
